\fBdefine(\|\fR[\fIparameter\|\fR[\fB\|,\|\fIparameter\|.\|.\|.\|\fR]\|]\|\fB)\|{\fI
	statements\|\fB}\fR
.fi
.PP
The define statement defines a function.
The parameters may
be ordinary identifiers or array names.
Array names must be followed by empty square brackets.
.NH 2
